.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
An independently animated part owned by a \fBSprite\fP\&. 

Independently animated \fBSprite\fP subsection, artwork holder, or mounting frame\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Create a \fBPart\fP by calling \fBcreatePart()\fP on a \fBSprite\fP instance\&. \fBPart\fP cannot be constructed directly with \fRnew\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const sprite = new pdg\&.Sprite();
const part = sprite\&.createPart("hand");
part\&.moveTo(new pdg\&.Point(12, 0), 0\&.25, pdg\&.easeInOutQuad);
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBPart\fP inherits \fBAnimated\fP's programmed movement, rotation and size operations\&. All animation durations are floating-point seconds\&. The owning \fBSprite\fP advances its attached Parts; do not also call \fBanimate()\fP on an attached \fBPart\fP every frame\&.

.PP
\fBBone\fP binding is optional\&. \fBgetBoneId()\fP is safe on an unbound \fBPart\fP and returns \fR\fBpdg\&.boneId_None\fP\fP\&. Binding and hierarchy belong to \fBPart\fP, not \fBAnimated\fP\&. \fBPart\fP has an optional \fBPhysicsBody\fP through its physics property\&. \fBsetupPhysicsBody()\fP creates it explicitly; otherwise physics returns \fBpdg\&.PhysicsBody\&.NoPhysics\fP\&. Only \fBsetupPhysicsBody()\fP/removePhysicsBody() can change the property association\&. Compare physics with \fBpdg\&.PhysicsBody\&.NoPhysics\fP to test absence\&. Removing a \fBPart\fP detaches its body and stops automatic stepping\&.

.PP
A retained \fBPart\fP remains valid after removal from its \fBSprite\fP; \fBisAttached()\fP reports false and its independent local transform remains available\&.

.PP
Create a \fBPart\fP with Sprite::createPart(name); names are unique within that \fBSprite\fP\&. Its local transform is relative to the \fBSprite\fP, an explicit parent \fBPart\fP, or an authored bone, binding or socket\&. \fBsetParentPart()\fP, \fBbindToBone()\fP, \fBbindToAnimationBinding()\fP and \fBbindToAnimationSocket()\fP select one frame without changing local offsets\&. \fBgetBoneId()\fP is always safe and returns boneId_None for an unbound \fBPart\fP (including one whose parent follows a bone)\&. Authored relationships are scoped to the current rig and safely invalidate on replacement\&.

.PP
\fBsetDrawing()\fP retains shared editable \fBDrawing\fP contents\&. setImage(image,localBounds) retains an image in an explicit local rectangle\&. Artwork changes leave identity, logical dimensions, programmed motion, parent/binding and physics untouched\&. \fBclearContent()\fP removes artwork\&. \fBgetContentBounds()\fP returns current artwork-local bounds or transformed bounds in partSpace_Sprite/partSpace_World\&. \fBPart\fP content is drawn after the owner's existing artwork, in \fBPart\fP creation order, with the owner's opacity and composed affine transform\&. Imported bindings supply transforms; this API does not duplicate or automatically replace imported artwork\&. \fBDrawing\fP still copies \fBAttributes\fP for its individual elements\&.
.SH "Attaching an independent Sprite"
.PP
hostPart\&.attachSprite(child, placement, childMount) returns a new \fBPart\fP beneath hostPart\&. This mounting \fBPart\fP retains the child and supplies an \fBAnimated\fP attachment offset; \fBgetAttachedSprite()\fP and child\&.getAttachmentPart() query the relationship\&. Animate the mounting \fBPart\fP to move the held object\&. The child root rejects competing transform edits, while its own clips, internal Parts, opacity and layer order remain independent\&. Attachment neither merges \fBPart\fP ownership nor steps the child twice\&.

.PP
partPlacement_Snap aligns the child's origin, or the optional childMount frame, with the host\&. partPlacement_PreserveWorld keeps its current world placement\&. childMount must belong to the child; its frame is sampled once when attaching\&. The mount's local state is the only editable attachment offset\&. \fBdetachSprite()\fP releases the child with its last published world pose and leaves the mounting \fBPart\fP available for reuse as an ordinary \fBPart\fP\&. Removal of the host socket or owning \fBSprite\fP also detaches\&. Layer removal currently detaches mounts because placement and update scheduling require a shared layer\&. JavaScript references retain Parts and Sprites automatically\&.

.PP
Both Sprites must share a layer (or both be outside layers)\&. Cycles, an already mounted child, singular placement, or a root transform requiring shear are rejected before creating a mount\&. Independent \fBPart\fP artwork supports affine shear, but \fBSprite\fP roots do not\&. A later invalid follow placement holds the last valid child pose and reports \fBgetAttachmentError()\fP; valid placement clears it\&. Use uniform ancestor scales or aligned axes when rotating mounts\&. Rigid attachments currently require a child without a \fBPhysicsBody\fP; physical holding constraints are not supported by this attachment API\&. Release does not invent physical velocity\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const socket = hero\&.createPart("weaponGrip");
socket\&.bindToAnimationSocket("grip");
const held = socket\&.attachSprite(sword, pdg\&.partPlacement_Snap);
held\&.rotateTo(0\&.3, 0\&.25, pdg\&.easeInOutQuad);
held\&.detachSprite();
.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Explicit Part-chain IK"
.PP
solveIK(middle,tip,target,space,bendDirection,influence) solves two segments whose joint offsets come from the local locations of a contiguous three-Part chain\&. It requires neither artwork nor bones\&. The target defaults to owning-layer/world coordinates; partSpace_Local means the root \fBPart\fP's parent frame\&. The root's local scale must have equal absolute axes; ancestor transforms may be affine/reflected\&. The bend direction is +1 or -1, and influence is in [0,1]\&. Unreachable targets clamp to the available reach and return false\&. Invalid topology or dynamic bodies reject the operation before changing either joint\&. Direct IK replaces rotation programming; \fBsetIKTarget()\fP and \fBsetIKDriveTarget()\fP install recurring controllers, and \fBsetIKLimits()\fP supplies fixed or shared rotary limits\&. Controller takeover requires explicit release with \fBclearIKTarget()\fP\&.
.SH "Part bodies"
.PP
An unbound \fBPart\fP can create its own \fBPhysicsBody\fP without a \fBSprite\fP root body\&. It joins the Chipmunk world on a physics-enabled layer and publishes the solved state once; removal detaches the retained body back to basic integration\&. This currently covers free bodies, shared constraints, contact reporting and kinematic target scheduling\&. Use \fBsetupCollider()\fP for explicit geometry, \fBsetupFrameCollider()\fP for owned artwork or an explicitly selected image binding, and setupAnimationCollider(boxName) for one authored box\&. \fBBone\fP binding alone does not create a physical joint or give the body authority to write a bone\&. Generated animation physics requires Chipmunk\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "boolean animate (number deltaSeconds)"

.SS "\fBPart\fP attachSprite (\fBSprite\fP child, int placement, \fBPart\fP childMount)"

.PP
Mount an independent \fBSprite\fP on this \fBPart\fP\&. Creates a new child \fBPart\fP beneath this host\&. The returned mounting \fBPart\fP controls the attachment offset; animate it rather than the child \fBSprite\fP's root\&. The child's clips, internal Parts, opacity, and layer order remain independent\&. Existing root motion/tweens and physical velocity are canceled when attaching\&. A mounted kinematic body follows the same target; direct body teleport, velocity edits, and changes out of kinematic mode throw until detachment\&. In a Chipmunk layer, the target is evaluated before the solve and its sweep velocity participates in contacts\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIchild\fP \fBSprite\fP to retain and mount\&. It must share the host's layer (or both must be outside layers), have no \fBPhysicsBody\fP or a body in physicsBody_Kinematic mode, and not already be attached\&. 
.br
\fIplacement\fP \fBpdg\&.partPlacement_Snap\fP aligns origins; \fBpdg\&.partPlacement_PreserveWorld\fP preserves the child's current world placement\&. 
.br
\fIchildMount\fP Optional \fBPart\fP belonging to the child\&. Its frame is sampled once as the child's mounting point instead of its origin\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A new mounting \fBPart\fP owned by the host's \fBSprite\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
To mount a physical \fBSprite\fP, create its body and set physicsBody_Kinematic before attaching\&. Cycles, singular transforms, and child-root transforms requiring shear are rejected before creating a mount\&. Removing the host from its layer removes the whole mounted group while preserving the mounts\&. Adding the host to another layer carries its descendants; detach a child before moving it independently\&. Layer coordinates are preserved during transfer\&. Use uniform ancestor scale or aligned axes when rotating attachments\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBdetachSprite()\fP, \fBgetAttachedSprite()\fP, \fBgetAttachmentError()\fP, \fBSprite::getAttachmentPart()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP attachSprite (\fBSprite\fP child, int placement = \fR\fBpartPlacement_Snap\fP\fP)"

.PP
Mount an independent \fBSprite\fP on this \fBPart\fP\&. Creates a new child \fBPart\fP beneath this host\&. The returned mounting \fBPart\fP controls the attachment offset; animate it rather than the child \fBSprite\fP's root\&. The child's clips, internal Parts, opacity, and layer order remain independent\&. Existing root motion/tweens and physical velocity are canceled when attaching\&. A mounted kinematic body follows the same target; direct body teleport, velocity edits, and changes out of kinematic mode throw until detachment\&. In a Chipmunk layer, the target is evaluated before the solve and its sweep velocity participates in contacts\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIchild\fP \fBSprite\fP to retain and mount\&. It must share the host's layer (or both must be outside layers), have no \fBPhysicsBody\fP or a body in physicsBody_Kinematic mode, and not already be attached\&. 
.br
\fIplacement\fP \fBpdg\&.partPlacement_Snap\fP aligns origins; \fBpdg\&.partPlacement_PreserveWorld\fP preserves the child's current world placement\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A new mounting \fBPart\fP owned by the host's \fBSprite\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
To mount a physical \fBSprite\fP, create its body and set physicsBody_Kinematic before attaching\&. Cycles, singular transforms, and child-root transforms requiring shear are rejected before creating a mount\&. Removing the host from its layer removes the whole mounted group while preserving the mounts\&. Adding the host to another layer carries its descendants; detach a child before moving it independently\&. Layer coordinates are preserved during transfer\&. Use uniform ancestor scale or aligned axes when rotating attachments\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const mount = grip\&.attachSprite(sword, pdg\&.partPlacement_Snap);
mount\&.rotateTo(0\&.3, 0\&.25, pdg\&.easeInOutQuad);
// Later: mount\&.detachSprite();

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBdetachSprite()\fP, \fBgetAttachedSprite()\fP, \fBgetAttachmentError()\fP, \fBSprite::getAttachmentPart()\fP 
.RE
.PP

