.SS "\fBPart\fP bindToBone (uint boneId)"

.PP
Follow a bone while preserving local offsets\&. Replaces the explicit parent and any previous authored binding\&. Local animation remains an offset from the selected frame\&. Invalid bone IDs and dynamic-body reparenting throw before changing the binding\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIboneId\fP Zero-based bone ID in the owner's current rig, or \fBpdg\&.boneId_None\fP to unbind\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The owning \fBSprite\fP must have an enabled animation pose and the selected bone\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const boneId = sprite\&.getAnimationBoneNames()\&.indexOf('hand');
part\&.bindToBone(boneId);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetBoneId()\fP, \fBunbindFromBone()\fP 
.RE
.PP

