.SS "\fBPart\fP clearIKTarget ()"

.PP
Stop this root’s scheduled IK controller\&. Keeps the current pose, clears its error and reached status, and releases its rotation channels for later programming\&. Physical IK also clears and releases its body drives while retaining velocities and independent loads\&. Harmless when no controller is registered\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetIKTarget()\fP 
.RE
.PP

