.SS "\fBRect\fP getContentBounds (int space = \fR\fBpartSpace_Local\fP\fP)"

.PP
Read the artwork bounds\&. Returns drawing geometry bounds\&. In \fBSprite\fP or World space, returns an axis-aligned rectangle around the transformed corners\&. Stroke extents may extend beyond these geometry bounds\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIspace\fP Integer \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_Local\fP\fP, \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_Sprite\fP\fP, or \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_World\fP\fP constant\&. World coordinates belong to the owning layer\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A new \fBRect\fP, or an empty \fBRect\fP when there is no artwork\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetDrawing()\fP, \fBsetImage()\fP, \fBgetTransform()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::partSpace_Local\fP\&.
.SS "\fBFABRIKResult\fP getFABRIKResult ()"

.PP
Return the latest scheduled FABRIK diagnostics\&. See \fBprocedural_fabrik_options\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent value describing the controller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint getId ()"

.PP
Read the \fBPart\fP ID in its current owner\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An unsigned integer scoped to the owning \fBSprite\fP\&. The ID is not an index into the current list of Parts\&. \fBSprite\&.transferPart()\fP assigns a new ID in the destination; object identity and retained handles remain stable\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::getPart()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "string getIKError ()"

.PP
Read a scheduled IK configuration error\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The last scheduled solve error, or an empty string after registration, successful solving, or clearing\&. Unreachable targets and partial influence report no error; use \fBisIKTargetReached()\fP for their result\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetIKTarget()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getIKMaxAngle ()"

.PP
Read the maximum local IK rotation\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The upper bound in local radians, or zero without limits\&. A linked constraint is read live; an invalid link throws\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "number getIKMinAngle ()"

.PP
Read the minimum local IK rotation\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The lower bound in local radians, or zero without limits\&. A linked constraint is read live; an invalid link throws\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "string getJiggleError ()"

.PP
Return the last chain jiggle or FABRIK evaluation error\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An error message, or the empty string after successful evaluation\&. Target-mode errors are reported by \fBgetIKError()\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPartJiggleOptions\fP getJiggleOptions ()"

.PP
Return an independent configuration record\&. See \fBprocedural_jiggle_options\fP and \fBprocedural_jiggle_state\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent value describing the controller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBJiggleResult\fP getJiggleResult ()"

.PP
Return the most recently evaluated jiggle diagnostics\&. See \fBprocedural_jiggle_options\fP and \fBprocedural_jiggle_state\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent value describing the controller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBJiggleState\fP getJiggleState ()"

.PP
Return an independent numerical state snapshot\&. See \fBprocedural_jiggle_options\fP and \fBprocedural_jiggle_state\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent value describing the controller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "string getName ()"

.PP
Read the \fBPart\fP name\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The immutable name assigned when the \fBPart\fP was created\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBSprite::findPart()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP getParentPart ()"

.PP
Read the explicit \fBPart\fP parent\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The explicit parent \fBPart\fP, or null\&. Authored bone/binding/socket parents are queried separately\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetParentPart()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBSprite\fP getSprite ()"

.PP
Read the owning \fBSprite\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The owner, or null after this \fBPart\fP is removed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBisAttached()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBAffineTransform\fP getTransform (int space = \fR\fBpartSpace_Local\fP\fP)"

.PP
Copy the \fBPart\fP's affine transform\&. Combines the requested parent/owner transforms\&. A detached \fBPart\fP retains its local frame\&. Invalid space constants throw\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIspace\fP Integer \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_Local\fP\fP, \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_Sprite\fP\fP, or \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_World\fP\fP constant\&. World coordinates belong to the owning layer\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent object with a, b, c, d, tx, and ty fields\&. Editing the object does not change the \fBPart\fP\&.
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBPart transform fields\fP
.RS 4
Field  Meaning  \fRa\fP, \fRb\fP, \fRc\fP, \fRd\fP  Linear part of the affine matrix; may include scale, reflection, and shear\&.  \fRtx\fP, \fRty\fP  Translation in the selected space\&.  
.RE
.PP
A local point (x, y) maps to (a*x + c*y + tx, b*x + d*y + ty)\&. Logical width, height, and center offset do not redefine a \fBPart\fP's frame\&.

.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetParentPart()\fP, \fBgetContentBounds()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::partSpace_Local\fP\&.
.SS "boolean hasContent ()"

.PP
Test whether artwork is assigned\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True when a \fBDrawing\fP or image has been assigned, even if its drawing is empty\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetDrawing()\fP, \fBsetImage()\fP, \fBclearContent()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean hasIKLimits ()"

.PP
Check whether this joint has IK rotation limits\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True when \fBsetIKLimits()\fP has configured numeric limits or a constraint link, including an invalid or disconnected link\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean hasIKTarget ()"

.PP
Check whether this \fBPart\fP owns a scheduled IK controller\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True even while an invalidated controller is holding an error; false after clearing or root removal\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetIKTarget()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean hasJiggle ()"

.PP
Return whether this \fBPart\fP owns a jiggle controller\&. See \fBprocedural_jiggle_options\fP and \fBprocedural_jiggle_state\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent value describing the controller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isAttached ()"

.PP
Test whether a \fBSprite\fP owns this \fBPart\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True while owned and automatically updated by a \fBSprite\fP; false after removal\&. This does not test whether a child \fBSprite\fP is mounted\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetSprite()\fP, \fBgetAttachedSprite()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isBoundToBone ()"

.PP
Test for a current direct bone binding\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True when \fBgetBoneId()\fP is not \fBpdg\&.boneId_None\fP\&. Binding to an authored image/point/box or socket may also establish a bone ID\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetBoneId()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isIKDriven ()"

.PP
Check whether this \fBPart\fP owns a physical IK controller\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True for a configured physical IK controller, including while it holds a structural error; false for direct IK or no controller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isIKTargetReached ()"

.PP
Check whether the scheduled IK controller has reached its target\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
For direct IK, the result of the last scheduled solve, false before the first solve; later transform edits do not update it\&. For physical IK, whether the current physical endpoint reaches the target within tolerance, recomputed on each query\&. False without a controller or while it has a configuration error\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetIKTarget()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean isJiggleEnabled ()"

.PP
Return whether jiggle is enabled\&. See \fBprocedural_jiggle_options\fP and \fBprocedural_jiggle_state\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent value describing the controller\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP kickJiggle (\fBPartJiggleKick\fP kick)"

.PP
Add angular or target velocity\&. See \fBprocedural_jiggle_options\fP and \fBprocedural_jiggle_state\fP\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIkick\fP Chain joint plus angularVelocity, or target velocityX/velocityY in world units/second\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "removeCollider ()"

.PP
Remove this owner’s collider\&. Idempotent\&. Restores shared NoCollider, removes native shapes, clears contact callbacks and detaches retained handles\&. Detached geometric queries preserve the final transform\&. 
.SS "removePhysicsBody ()"

.PP
Detach the optional physics body\&. Restores the physics property to \fBPhysicsBody\&.NoPhysics\fP\&. A retained body keeps its state, loses its owner/solver, and can be advanced with \fBPhysicsBody\&.step()\fP\&. Calling when no body exists is harmless\&. A mapped rig body requires \fBSprite::disableAnimationPhysics()\fP first; otherwise this operation throws without removing it\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetupPhysicsBody()\fP, \fBPhysicsBody::step()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP resetJiggle ()"

.PP
Reseed jiggle from the desired pose or target\&. See \fBprocedural_jiggle_options\fP and \fBprocedural_jiggle_state\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP setDrawing (\fBDrawing\fP drawing)"

.PP
Assign editable \fBDrawing\fP artwork\&. Retains shared drawing contents, including later \fBElementRef\fP edits\&. Replaces existing content without changing the \fBPart\fP's name, logical dimensions, animation, parent frame, or physics body\&. Parts draw after the owner's original artwork, in creation order\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdrawing\fP \fBDrawing\fP whose geometry is expressed in this \fBPart\fP's local coordinates\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const artwork = pdg\&.createDrawing();
artwork\&.addRect(new pdg\&.Rect(0, \-2, 20, 2), new pdg\&.Attributes()\&.fillColor('white'));
part\&.setDrawing(artwork);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetImage()\fP, \fBclearContent()\fP, \fBgetContentBounds()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP setFABRIKTarget (\fBPart\fP[] chain, \fBPoint\fP target, \fBPartFABRIKOptions\fP options = \fRundefined\fP)"

.PP
Solve or schedule a contiguous independent \fBPart\fP chain; chain excludes the receiver\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fRchain:\fP Array of \fR\fBPart\fP\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
See \fBprocedural_fabrik_options\fP\&.

.PP
The last chain entry is the endpoint\&. Call again to update its target\&. Use \fBclearIKTarget()\fP to remove the scheduled solver\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIchain\fP Contiguous descendants, excluding this \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fItarget\fP Desired endpoint in the configured coordinate frame\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP Configuration described in the shared options reference\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP setIKDriveTarget (\fBPart\fP middle, \fBPart\fP tip, \fBPoint\fP target, number maxForce, number maxTorque, int space = \fR\fBpartSpace_World\fP\fP, int bendDirection = \fR1\fP, number influence = \fR1\fP, number frequency = \fR4\fP, number dampingRatio = \fR1\fP)"

.PP
Drive a two-segment \fBPart\fP chain toward an IK target using bounded forces and torques\&. Installs a persistent controller\&. Each step computes a desired pose after \fBPart\fP animation and before the physics solve\&. The solver retains authority over all physical positions and rotations; registering or updating a target does not teleport the chain\&. The root and middle must have independent dynamic bodies\&. The tip may have a dynamic body or no body\&. All three Parts must form a contiguous chain in one \fBSprite\fP\&. Imported physical-rig Parts are not supported by this controller\&.

.PP
The first assignment captures the root's parent-relative anchor and the middle and tip joint offsets\&. Repeated assignments to the same chain retain those values, so physical drift cannot redefine segment lengths\&. Clear and reinstall to capture a new chain configuration\&. Ancestor movement and the current \fBPart\fP scales still apply\&. The root requires uniform absolute scale, as with \fBsolveIK()\fP\&.

.PP
The controller owns each participating body drive until \fBclearIKTarget()\fP\&. Existing independent body drives or overlapping IK controllers cause setup to throw without replacing the old controller\&. Direct setDriveTarget(), clearDrive(), stopAllForces() and changes away from dynamic mode reject while the controller owns the body\&. Impulses and other forces may still disturb it\&. No joints are created implicitly: configure pivot joints, physical angular limits and collision shapes separately\&. Any pivot or pin between adjacent driven Parts must join the captured parent offset to the child origin (pin distance zero)\&. Mismatched anchors reject setup or suspend a running controller\&. Anchors are unscaled body-local coordinates; account for \fBPart\fP scaling when configuring them\&.

.PP
The root's target position is its captured anchor; the middle and physical tip receive the solved joint positions\&. Body orientations use the shortest rotation route, except joints sharing a rotary limit preserve its unwrapped relative angle so the drive does not request a shortcut through the physical stop\&. Force/torque caps apply separately to each body\&. A physical tip retains its captured local orientation relative to the desired middle pose\&. Influence zero turns off the controller's drive contribution without releasing ownership\&.

.PP
A missing/replaced body or invalid topology stops all this controller's drives and records \fBgetIKError()\fP\&. Valid topology can resume; after replacing a body, call \fBsetIKDriveTarget()\fP again to claim it\&. \fBisIKTargetReached()\fP measures the current physical endpoint, so a constrained or force-limited chain may remain unreached without a configuration error\&. Clearing preserves velocities, constraints and independently applied loads\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImiddle\fP This \fBPart\fP's immediate child, with a dynamic \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&. 
.br
\fItip\fP Middle's immediate child, with a dynamic body or no body\&. 
.br
\fItarget\fP Desired endpoint in the selected coordinate space\&. 
.br
\fImaxForce\fP Finite nonnegative force cap per driven body\&. 
.br
\fImaxTorque\fP Finite nonnegative torque cap per driven body\&. 
.br
\fIspace\fP partSpace_World by default; partSpace_Sprite or partSpace_Local (root's parent frame) are also accepted\&. 
.br
\fIbendDirection\fP +1 by default, or -1 for the other bend direction\&. 
.br
\fIinfluence\fP Pose influence from zero through one; default 1\&. 
.br
\fIfrequency\fP Positive drive frequency in cycles per second; default 4\&. 
.br
\fIdampingRatio\fP Nonnegative drive damping ratio; default 1\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Advance the owning \fBSpriteLayer\fP normally\&. Bodies use either the basic or Chipmunk solver; step size, constraints and force caps affect convergence\&. Initial Sprite/Layer snapshots preserve the controller, captured joint offsets, body drives and shared rotary limits in either resource mode\&. Save the containing Layer when a joint or compound collider references another \fBSprite\fP\&. Restored controllers retain exclusive ownership of their bodies and resume on the next step\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const shoulder = sprite\&.createPart("shoulder");
const elbow = sprite\&.createPart("elbow");
const wrist = sprite\&.createPart("wrist");
elbow\&.setParentPart(shoulder)\&.setLocation(10, 0);
wrist\&.setParentPart(elbow)\&.setLocation(8, 0);
shoulder\&.setupPhysicsBody(1, 20);
elbow\&.setupPhysicsBody(1, 20);
shoulder\&.physics\&.createPivotJoint(elbow\&.physics, new pdg\&.Point(10, 0));
const elbowLimit = shoulder\&.physics\&.createRotaryLimit(elbow\&.physics, 0, 2\&.5);
elbow\&.setIKLimits(elbowLimit);
shoulder\&.setIKDriveTarget(elbow, wrist, new pdg\&.Point(10, 8), 100, 40,
                         pdg\&.partSpace_Sprite);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetIKTarget()\fP, \fBsetIKLimits()\fP, \fBclearIKTarget()\fP, \fBPhysicsBody::setDriveTarget()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::partSpace_World\fP\&.
.SS "\fBPart\fP setIKLimits (number minAngle, number maxAngle)"

.PP
Limit this joint's local rotation when solving \fBPart\fP IK\&. Angles are radians in the \fBPart\fP's parent frame\&. Both bounds must be finite, representable as \fBPart\fP rotations, and ordered, spanning at most one full turn\&. Equal bounds lock the desired angle\&. The interval may cross a multiple of a full turn by using unwrapped values, such as 6\&.0 through 6\&.5\&. Invalid input leaves the old limits intact\&. This configuration does not immediately rotate the \fBPart\fP or constrain ordinary \fBAnimated\fP calls\&.

.PP
Set limits on the root and/or middle \fBPart\fP\&. Direct and persistent IK honor them; physical IK limits its desired pose\&. Physical bodies can overshoot or be pushed outside that pose: use \fBPhysicsBody::createRotaryLimit()\fP for a physical constraint\&. When both bend solutions satisfy the limits, bendDirection selects the preferred one\&. Otherwise the solve chooses the nearest permitted endpoint in the chain's parent coordinate frame\&. Positive partial influence remains inside the allowed interval\&. Numeric limits replace any live constraint link and are included in ordinary \fBPart\fP snapshots in both resource modes\&. Use the \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP overload to share an existing physical limit\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIminAngle\fP Minimum local rotation, in radians\&. 
.br
\fImaxAngle\fP Maximum local rotation, in radians\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBclearIKLimits()\fP, \fBsolveIK()\fP, \fBsetIKDriveTarget()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP setIKLimits (\fBPhysicsConstraint\fP constraint)"

.PP
Share a live physical rotary limit with this IK joint\&. Retains the constraint and reads its current interval on each solve and limit query\&. Changing \fBPhysicsConstraint::setAngleLimits()\fP changes the physical limit and the IK range together\&. This replaces any numeric or linked IK limits without changing the pose, creating bodies, or creating joints\&.

.PP
The active constraint must connect this \fBPart\fP's body to its immediate parent \fBPart\fP's body, or to the owning \fBSprite\fP's body for a root \fBPart\fP\&. Either endpoint order is accepted: reversed endpoints negate and exchange the bounds, so IK queries still report this \fBPart\fP's rotation relative to its parent\&.

.PP
The parent frame must be uniform, unreflected, and aligned with the parent body's orientation\&. This \fBPart\fP must have positive effective scale axes\&. Authored source frames on a root \fBPart\fP and imported physical-rig bodies are unsupported\&. The interval must fit \fBPart\fP rotations and span at most one turn\&. Invalid setup leaves the old configuration intact\&. These conditions are checked again when used\&.

.PP
If the constraint breaks, disconnects, changes to an unsupported interval, or no longer connects the correct bodies, direct solves and angle queries throw\&. Persistent IK records \fBgetIKError()\fP and holds its pose; physical IK stops all its owned drives\&. The link remains configured, so \fBhasIKLimits()\fP stays true\&. Clear or replace it to recover; temporary frame/range errors recover when corrected\&. Clearing the link does not disconnect the physical constraint\&. Its retained handle stays safe after body removal\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconstraint\fP An active \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP of type constraint_RotaryLimit\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Initial Sprite/Layer snapshots retain the live constraint link\&. Save the containing Layer if its constraint endpoints span Sprites\&. Disconnected links and invalid live configurations must be cleared or repaired before saving\&. Numeric limits also round-trip without physics\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsConstraint::setAngleLimits()\fP, \fBclearIKLimits()\fP, \fBsetIKDriveTarget()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPart\fP setIKTarget (\fBPart\fP middle, \fBPart\fP tip, \fBPoint\fP target, int space = \fR\fBpartSpace_World\fP\fP, int bendDirection = \fR1\fP, number influence = \fR1\fP)"

.PP
Maintain a target for a contiguous two-segment \fBPart\fP chain\&. Registers or replaces this root's controller without changing the current pose\&. During a \fBSprite\fP step, all Parts advance their local animation and callbacks first; controllers then run in parent-before-child order, followed by physical publication\&. Calling \fBanimate()\fP directly on this \fBPart\fP also runs its controller after its own local animation\&. Do not manually step Parts that their \fBSprite\fP already updates\&.

.PP
The solver uses the same joint offsets, coordinate spaces, scale rules, elbow side, and influence as \fBsolveIK()\fP\&. Positive influence replaces rotation tweens and spin on this root and the middle joint when solving\&. Controllers that would write the same joint are rejected before replacing an existing registration\&. Independent chains may coexist\&. The target remains active until \fBclearIKTarget()\fP or removal of this root\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImiddle\fP Direct child of this \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fItip\fP Direct child of middle, in the same \fBSprite\fP\&. 
.br
\fItarget\fP Finite target position in the selected space\&. 
.br
\fIspace\fP partSpace_Local (root's parent frame), partSpace_Sprite, or partSpace_World (owning-layer coordinates)\&. Defaults to World\&. 
.br
\fIbendDirection\fP Integer +1 or -1 selecting elbow side; defaults to +1\&. 
.br
\fIinfluence\fP Finite amount in [0,1], default 1\&. Partial influence approaches the goal on successive solves\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires valid contiguous joints, nonzero segment lengths, nonsingular parent transforms and equal absolute root scale axes\&. Dynamic bodies reject direct IK; this controller supports nonphysical and kinematic Parts\&. It does not create physical joints or drives\&. If a later edit invalidates the chain, the controller holds its rotation edits and records \fBgetIKError()\fP; valid geometry resumes solving\&. An unreachable target clamps to the available reach and is not a configuration error\&.
.RE
.PP
Initial Sprite/Layer snapshots preserve the controller configuration, \fBPart\fP IDs, last reached status and error text in both resource modes\&. Links are resolved after all Parts, parents and bodies exist\&. Invalid live configurations reject saving; malformed controller references reject restoration before replacing the \fBPart\fP graph\&.

.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const shoulder = sprite\&.createPart('shoulder');
const elbow = sprite\&.createPart('elbow');
const wrist = sprite\&.createPart('wrist');
elbow\&.setParentPart(shoulder)\&.setLocation(new pdg\&.Point(10, 0));
wrist\&.setParentPart(elbow)\&.setLocation(new pdg\&.Point(8, 0));
shoulder\&.setIKTarget(elbow, wrist, new pdg\&.Point(12, 8), pdg\&.partSpace_Sprite);
// The Sprite's regular animation step keeps solving toward this target\&.
// Later: shoulder\&.clearIKTarget();

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsolveIK()\fP, \fBclearIKTarget()\fP, \fBhasIKTarget()\fP, \fBisIKTargetReached()\fP, \fBgetIKError()\fP 
.RE
.PP

