.SS "\fBCollider\fP setupAnimationCollider (string boxName)"

.PP
Select one authored animation box as this \fBPart\fP's collision source\&. boxName must identify a box in the owning \fBSprite\fP's enabled animation pose; image and point bindings are rejected\&. The \fBPart\fP need not already be bound\&. Setup aligns the shape with the authored box, accounting for the \fBPart\fP's local transform at setup\&. Playback and the final pose update the box relative to the \fBPart\fP's current parent frame; subsequent local \fBPart\fP edits carry that shape\&. Singular parent frames yield no source shape until invertible again\&. A singular local transform at setup throws\&.

.PP
The box name is explicit: unlike \fBSprite\&.setupAnimationCollider()\fP, this method does not collect every box\&. Inactive boxes have no shape; reappearing boxes keep their source ID\&. Explicit \fBCollider\fP additions remain alongside the source\&.

.PP
Replacing/disabling the pose or transferring the \fBPart\fP to another \fBSprite\fP retires the old source without silently rebinding it\&. Select a current source before saving that \fBPart\fP; snapshots reject stale authored sources\&. Valid snapshots in both resource modes retain the selected box, setup offset and source IDs\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIboxName\fP Required, exact authored box name; empty or unknown names throw\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP's \fBCollider\fP\&. JavaScript retains the returned handle\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Requires Spriter support and an enabled owner pose, in GUI or headless builds\&. No physics body or Chipmunk solver is required for collider queries\&. Setup preserves configuration and replaces geometry, like \fBsetupFrameCollider()\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4
The enabled pose on hero contains a hand bone and a hitbox box\&. 
.PP
.nf
const hand = hero\&.getAnimationBoneNames()\&.indexOf('hand');
const hit = hero\&.createPart('handHit')\&.bindToBone(hand);
hit\&.setupAnimationCollider('hitbox')\&.setSensor(true);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetupFrameCollider()\fP, \fBSprite::setupAnimationCollider()\fP, \fBbindToBone()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBCollider\fP setupCollider ()"

.PP
Set up the collision geometry association for this owner\&. An existing collider keeps its geometry and settings; use \&.collider to access it directly\&. A new collider starts enabled with no shapes, no sensor flag and owner-body association\&. Does not create a \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The owned collider\&. Native callers may addRef()/release() to retain it after removal\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBCollider\fP setupFrameCollider (int mode = \fR\fBframeCollider_AlphaMask\fP\fP, int alphaThreshold = \fR128\fP)"

.PP
Set up collision geometry from this \fBPart\fP's current artwork\&. Reuses \&.collider when present, preserving its configuration, filters, material, handlers and body association\&. Each call replaces the previous geometry source and explicit shapes\&. Later \fBCollider\fP add methods create persistent extra shapes\&. Queries and contacts refresh source geometry; source shape IDs survive artwork changes and disappearance/reappearance\&. See \fBcollider_geometry_sources\fP\&.

.PP
Owned \fBDrawing\fP content takes precedence\&. Bounds uses its current local bounding rectangle, including element transforms\&. AlphaMask requires exactly one image or image-strip element using fit_Fill; \fBsetImage()\fP supplies suitable content\&. It samples the selected \fBAttributes\&.frame()\fP, with an invalid frame falling back to zero as in drawing\&. Alpha ignores stroke, fill overlays and opacity effects\&. Pixel edits to an existing \fBImage\fP require calling \fBsetupFrameCollider()\fP again\&. Unsupported vector/multi-element/other-fit alpha sources throw; use Bounds for those Drawings\&. Replacing content later with an unsupported alpha source also causes source queries to throw until corrected or another source is selected\&.

.PP
Without owned content, an explicitly bound animation image (from \fBbindToAnimationBinding()\fP) supplies its current frame and pivot\&. A bone or socket binding alone does not select artwork\&. No artwork produces no source shapes; logical \fBPart\fP width/height do not invent a frame\&. \fBPart\fP transforms, including reflection, apply normally\&. Artwork changes do not change body mass or inertia\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImode\fP frameCollider_AlphaMask (default) or frameCollider_Bounds\&. 
.br
\fIalphaThreshold\fP Integer 1 through 255, default 128; alpha at or above this value collides\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBPart\fP's \fBCollider\fP\&. JavaScript retains the returned handle\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Owned image/Drawing content and imported image-frame adapters require a GUI-capable build\&. Enable layer collisions for contacts; queries work without a layer or body\&. Invalid setup preserves the previous collider/source\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4
The enabled pose on hero contains an image binding named hand_art\&. 
.PP
.nf
const grip = hero\&.createPart('gripArt')\&.bindToAnimationBinding('hand_art');
const collider = grip\&.setupFrameCollider(pdg\&.frameCollider_AlphaMask);
collider\&.setSensor(true);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetupAnimationCollider()\fP, \fBsetDrawing()\fP, \fBsetImage()\fP, \fBCollider\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
References \fBpdg::frameCollider_AlphaMask\fP\&.
.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setupPhysicsBody (number mass = \fR1\fP, number momentOfInertia = \fR1\fP)"

.PP
Set up the optional physics body with the specified mass and inertia\&. Every call applies both arguments, including their defaults: \fBsetupPhysicsBody()\fP sets mass and moment of inertia to 1, and setupPhysicsBody(5) sets mass to 5 and inertia to 1\&. An existing body keeps its identity, transform, velocity, mode, forces, constraints and other settings\&. Read \&.physics to access it without reconfiguration\&. Invalid mass or inertia throws before changing either value\&.

.PP
If absent, creates a dynamic body at the owner's current transform and stops programmed movement/spin\&. Removal detaches retained references; JavaScript keeps them alive automatically\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImass\fP Finite positive mass; default 1\&. 
.br
\fImomentOfInertia\fP Finite positive moment of inertia; default 1\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The owner's \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&. The read-only physics property refers to this same object\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parts created by \fBSprite::setupAnimationPhysics()\fP use their solved bone and fixed capsule offset\&. Their immediate transform edits, rebinding, reparenting and removal require disabling the rig first; operate on their \fR\&.\fBphysics\fP\fP bodies to control physical motion\&.

.PP
Dynamic bodies own movement and rotation\&. Programmed movement/spin requests on their owners throw; immediate setters teleport the body\&. Dynamic and static Parts retain their world position as ancestors move; kinematic Parts follow their animated parent frame\&. Physical transforms publish in parent-before-child order after authored animation\&. Local artwork may have zero scale, but a physical \fBPart\fP requires an invertible parent frame\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const body = part\&.setupPhysicsBody(2, 4);
body\&.applyImpulse(new pdg\&.Vector(4, 0));

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBremovePhysicsBody()\fP, \fBPhysicsBody\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBFABRIKResult\fP solveFABRIK (\fBPart\fP[] chain, \fBPoint\fP target, \fBPartFABRIKOptions\fP options = \fRundefined\fP)"

.PP
Solve or schedule a contiguous independent \fBPart\fP chain; chain excludes the receiver\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fRchain:\fP Array of \fR\fBPart\fP\fP\&.
