.SS "boolean solveIK (\fBPart\fP middle, \fBPart\fP tip, \fBPoint\fP target, int space = \fR\fBpartSpace_World\fP\fP, int bendDirection = \fR1\fP, number influence = \fR1\fP)"

.PP
Aim a contiguous two-segment \fBPart\fP chain\&. Rotates this \fBPart\fP and its middle child to bring the tip toward the target\&. Segment lengths come from the child joint offsets, not artwork dimensions\&. Unreachable targets clamp to available reach\&. With positive influence, this replaces rotation tweens and spin on the two solved joints\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImiddle\fP Direct child of this \fBPart\fP\&. 
.br
\fItip\fP Direct child of middle, in the same \fBSprite\fP\&. 
.br
\fItarget\fP Finite target position in the selected space\&. 
.br
\fIspace\fP Integer \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_Local\fP\fP, \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_Sprite\fP\fP, or \fR\fBpdg\&.partSpace_World\fP\fP constant\&. World coordinates belong to the owning layer\&. For this solver, Local means this root \fBPart\fP's parent frame\&. 
.br
\fIbendDirection\fP Integer +1 or -1 selecting the elbow side\&. 
.br
\fIinfluence\fP Finite blend amount from 0 (unchanged) to 1 (full solve)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True when the resulting tip reaches the target within tolerance; false when it cannot, including partial influence\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
All three Parts must share a \fBSprite\fP and form a direct chain\&. The root scale must be nonzero with equal absolute axes\&. Zero-length segments, singular parent frames, and dynamic bodies are rejected before changing either joint\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const root = sprite\&.createPart('armRoot');
const middle = sprite\&.createPart('elbow');
const tip = sprite\&.createPart('handTip');
middle\&.setParentPart(root)\&.setLocation(new pdg\&.Point(10, 0));
tip\&.setParentPart(middle)\&.setLocation(new pdg\&.Point(8, 0));
root\&.solveIK(middle, tip, new pdg\&.Point(12, 8), pdg\&.partSpace_Sprite);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetParentPart()\fP, \fBgetTransform()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
